<title>USA: Former &quot;Today&quot; host Gumbel heading to CBS - report.</title>
<headline>Former &quot;Today&quot; host Gumbel heading to CBS - report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bryant Gumbel, who anchored NBC's &quot;Today&quot; show for 15 years before leaving in January, will be joining CBS, the Daily Variety reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper said Gumbel is joining the network for a $5 million-a-year paycheck that includes stock options in the company.</p>
<p>CBS recruited Gumbel, one of the most prominent black journalists on television, after nearly a year of courtship, the paper said.</p>
<p>Westinghouse owns CBS, and General Electric owns NBC.</p>
